# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# These rules are CUMULATIVE, not cascading. When two blocks match the same
# request, Cloudflare joins the values with a comma instead of letting the more
# specific block win. Setting Cache-Control in both /* and /_astro/* produced:
#
#   public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# and a cache that reads the first max-age it finds treats a fingerprinted asset
# as uncacheable, which is the exact opposite of the intent. So the asset block
# unsets the inherited value with "!" before setting its own.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Astro fingerprints every asset it emits (_slug_.BpychFDU.css), so a changed
# file always arrives under a new name and can be cached indefinitely. The HTML
# above is never cached, so a deploy is visible immediately.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
